---
import DocumentationLayout from '@/layouts/DocumentationLayout.astro'
---

<DocumentationLayout
  title="SDK Guide"
  description="Install and use the TypeScript and Python SDKs auto-generated from OpenAPI"
>
  <h1>SDK Guide</h1>

  <p>
    The Pixelated Empathy SDKs are auto-generated from our
    <a href="/docs/api/_openapi.yaml">OpenAPI 3.1 specification</a> using
    <a href="https://openapi-generator.tech/">openapi-generator</a>. The
    generation pipeline runs automatically in CI whenever the spec changes.
  </p>

  <h2>Available SDKs</h2>

  <table class="sdk-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Language</th>
        <th>Package</th>
        <th>Registry</th>
        <th>Min Version</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>TypeScript</td>
        <td><code>@pixelated-empathy/auto-sdk</code></td>
        <td>npm</td>
        <td>Node.js 18+</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Python</td>
        <td><code>pixelated-empathy-sdk</code></td>
        <td>PyPI</td>
        <td>Python 3.9+</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>TypeScript SDK</h2>

  <h3>Installation</h3>
  <pre><code class="language-bash">npm install @pixelated-empathy/auto-sdk
# or
pnpm add @pixelated-empathy/auto-sdk</code></pre>

  <h3>Configuration</h3>
  <pre><code class="language-typescript" is:raw>import {
  Configuration,
  DefaultApi,
} from '@pixelated-empathy/auto-sdk';

const config = new Configuration({
  // Required: API key from /admin/api-keys
  apiKey: process.env.PIXELATED_API_KEY,

  // Optional: Override base URL (default: https://api.pixelatedempathy.com)
  basePath: process.env.PIXELATED_API_URL ?? 'https://api.pixelatedempathy.com',

  // Optional: Request timeout (default: 30000ms)
  timeout: 30000,

  // Optional: Retry configuration
  retry: {
    maxRetries: 3,
    initialDelayMs: 500,
    maxDelayMs: 5000,
    retryOnStatus: [429, 500, 502, 503],
  },
});

const client = new DefaultApi(config);</code></pre>

  <h3>Using the Client</h3>
  <pre><code class="language-typescript" is:raw>// All methods are typed with auto-generated interfaces
const health = await client.getHealth();
//    ^? { status: string; version: string; timestamp: string }

const search = await client.searchContent({
  q: 'anxiety',
  limit: 10,
  offset: 0,
});
//    ^? { data: SearchResult[]; total: number; page: number }

// Type-safe request and response objects
const memory = await client.createMemory({
  userId: 'user-123',
  content: 'Session notes',
  metadata: { sessionType: 'cbt' },
});
//    ^? { id: string; userId: string; content: string; createdAt: string }</code></pre>

  <h2>Python SDK</h2>

  <h3>Installation</h3>
  <pre><code class="language-bash">pip install pixelated-empathy-sdk
# or
uv add pixelated-empathy-sdk</code></pre>

  <h3>Configuration</h3>
  <pre><code class="language-python">import os
from pixelated_empathy_sdk import Configuration, DefaultApi

config = Configuration(
    api_key=os.environ["PIXELATED_API_KEY"],
    host=os.environ.get("PIXELATED_API_URL", "https://api.pixelatedempathy.com"),
    timeout=30000,
)

client = DefaultApi(config)</code></pre>

  <h3>Using the Client</h3>
  <pre><code class="language-python"># All methods are typed with auto-generated interfaces
health = client.get_health()
print(health.status, health.version)

search = client.search_content(q="anxiety", limit=10, offset=0)
for result in search.data:
    print(result.id, result.title)

# Type-safe request and response objects
memory = client.create_memory(
    user_id="user-123",
    content="Session notes",
    metadata={"sessionType": "cbt"},
)
print(memory.id, memory.created_at)</code></pre>

  <h2>Hand-Written SDK (Legacy)</h2>
  <p>
    A hand-written TypeScript SDK (<code>@pixelated-empathy/sdk</code>) is
    also available at <code>packages/pixelated-sdk/</code>. It provides
    additional features like Zod schema validation and a fluent API. The
    auto-generated SDK is recommended for new integrations as it stays
    in sync with the OpenAPI spec automatically.
  </p>

  <h2>SDK Generation Pipeline</h2>
  <p>
    The SDK generation pipeline runs in CI at
    <code>.github/workflows/sdk-generation.yml</code>. It:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Validates the OpenAPI spec with Spectral linting</li>
    <li>Downloads <code>openapi-generator-cli</code> v7.12.0</li>
    <li>Generates TypeScript (typescript-fetch) and Python SDKs</li>
    <li>Builds and type-checks both packages</li>
    <li>Publishes to npm and PyPI on <code>main</code> branch</li>
    <li>Uploads generated code as CI artifacts</li>
  </ol>

  <p>To regenerate SDKs manually:</p>
  <pre><code class="language-bash">./scripts/ci/generate-sdks.sh        # Generate only
./scripts/ci/generate-sdks.sh --publish  # Generate + publish</code></pre>

  <h2>Related</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/docs/developer/getting-started">Getting Started Guide</a></li>
    <li><a href="/docs/developer/code-examples">Code Examples</a></li>
    <li><a href="/docs/api/swagger">Interactive API Reference</a></li>
  </ul>
</DocumentationLayout>

<style>
  .sdk-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }

  th, td {
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    text-align: left;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
  }

  th {
    font-weight: 600;
    background: #f8fafc;
  }

  pre {
    background: #1e293b;
    color: #e2e8f0;
    padding: 1rem;
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  code {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace;
  }

  :not(pre) > code {
    background: #f1f5f9;
    padding: 0.125rem 0.375rem;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    font-size: 0.875em;
  }
</style>
